🐳 Top 20 Docker Interview Questions
Senior Java Developer (Spring Boot + AWS + Kubernetes)

These are the questions most commonly asked in banking and enterprise interviews and are heavily covered in your Docker preparation materials.

1. What is Docker?
Answer

Docker is a containerization platform used to package:

Application
+
Dependencies
+
Configuration


into a container.

One-Liner
Docker = Build Once, Run Anywhere.

2. Docker vs Virtual Machine
Docker	VMShares Host OS	Own Guest OS
Lightweight	Heavy
Starts in Seconds	Starts in Minutes
Less Memory	More Memory
One-Liner
Containers virtualize applications, VMs virtualize operating systems.

3. Image vs Container
Docker Image
Blueprint
Template
Read Only

Container
Running Instance
Of Image


Example

docker run nginx

One-Liner
Image = Class

Container = Object

4. Explain Docker Architecture
Docker Client
      ↓
Docker Daemon
      ↓
Images
      ↓
Containers
      ↓
Registry

One-Liner
Client sends commands, Daemon executes them.

5. What is Dockerfile?
Example
FROM eclipse-temurin:21

COPY app.jar app.jar

ENTRYPOINT
["java","-jar","app.jar"]

One-Liner
Dockerfile contains instructions to build Docker images.

6. How Do You Build An Image?
Command
docker build -t payment-app .

Explanation
-t = Tag
.  = Current Folder

One-Liner
docker build converts Dockerfile into image.

7. How Do You Run A Container?
Command
docker run payment-app


Port Mapping

docker run -p 8080:8080 payment-app

One-Liner
docker run creates container from image.

8. COPY vs ADD
COPY
COPY app.jar app.jar


Copies files only.

ADD
ADD my.zip /


Can:

Extract Archives

Download URLs

One-Liner
Use COPY whenever possible.

9. CMD vs ENTRYPOINT
CMD
CMD
["java","-jar","app.jar"]


Can be overridden.

ENTRYPOINT
ENTRYPOINT
["java","-jar","app.jar"]


Harder to override.

One-Liner
CMD = Default Command

ENTRYPOINT = Main Command

10. What Are Docker Volumes?
Problem
Container Deleted

Data Lost

Solution
docker volume create app-data

One-Liner
Volumes provide persistent storage.

11. Why Are Volumes Needed?

Without Volume

Container Deleted
     ↓
Data Deleted


With Volume

Container Deleted
     ↓
Data Safe

One-Liner
Volumes survive container restarts and deletion.

12. Docker Networking
Common Networks
Bridge

Host

Overlay

None

Example
docker network ls

One-Liner
Networking allows containers to communicate.

13. What Is Docker Compose?
Scenario

Need

Spring Boot

MySQL

Redis


Together.

docker-compose.yml
services:

  app:
    image: app

  mysql:
    image: mysql


Run

docker-compose up

One-Liner
Docker Compose manages multiple containers together.

14. What Is Multi-Stage Build?
Traditional
Build Tools
+
Application


Huge Image

Multi Stage
FROM maven:3.9 AS build

RUN mvn package

FROM eclipse-temurin:21

COPY --from=build app.jar app.jar

One-Liner
Multi-stage build reduces image size dramatically.

15. How To Reduce Docker Image Size?
Best Practices
Use Multi Stage Build

Use Slim Images

Use Alpine Images

Remove Temporary Files


Example

FROM eclipse-temurin:21-jre-alpine

One-Liner
Smaller image = Faster deployment.

16. How To Pass Environment Variables?
Dockerfile
ENV PROFILE=prod

Runtime
docker run -e DB_URL=mysql app

Spring Boot
docker run
-e SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=prod

One-Liner
Environment variables externalize configuration.

17. How To Debug Running Container?
Commands
docker ps

docker logs container-id

docker exec -it
container-id bash

Interview Answer
First Logs

Then Enter Container

Then Check Configuration

One-Liner
docker logs is usually the first troubleshooting command.

18. Push Image To Docker Hub / ECR
Docker Hub
docker push myrepo/app

AWS ECR
docker tag app:1.0 repo/app:1.0

docker push repo/app:1.0

One-Liner
Build → Tag → Push

19. Docker vs Kubernetes
Docker
Container Runtime

Kubernetes
Container Orchestration

Example
Docker
   ↓
Creates Container

Kubernetes
   ↓
Manages Containers

One-Liner
Docker runs containers, Kubernetes manages containers.

